                <pb facs="0484" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg388"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. St. Victor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 294.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Agreeable to the request made by your
                    Government that the gentlemen who have sought protection at our legation should
                    depart on the first steamer that should leave this port, these gentlemen will
                    depart on the German steamer which leaves to-day.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
